{
  "format": 1,
  "name": "flora_persistence",
  "spec": ["flora 10.1", "flora 10.2", "flora 8", "foundations 2.7"],
  "description": "Derived by hand from flora 10.1 and 10.2 (tests 27 and 28 of 16). A new 64^2 city with no burnt flora writes 2 (version) + 4 bools + 8 (sizes) + 8 (cells) + 16 (today, period, blocksPerMonth, wild seeds) + 1 (keepIteratorFlag) = 39, the iterator 3 + 16 + 4 + 4 + 2 * 1024 + 12 = 2087 (state 1 running, mode 0 table, dirty 1, rect 0, 0, 31, 31, count 1024, n 1024, index 0, current 0, step 1), the generator 20 (lcg, mul, cached flag 0, cached double), count 0 (4) and the accumulators (8): 2158 bytes, offsets checked below (1024.0f = 00 00 80 44, period 24, blocksPerMonth 42). A save after 'Flora propogation', 'Flora preserve', enabled := false, today 1234, two burnt trees and accumulators 0.25 / 0.5 loads into a simulator with a different seed and restores all of them (the burnt references resolve through the store; each loaded reference adds one host reference) and the generator: re-saving is byte-identical, and the next RandomDoubleUniform after two separate loads leaves byte-identical saves. Version 3 -> Read returns false after reading the 2-byte version. A burnt count of 10,000,000 -> Read clears the list ([choice] releasing its references), reads no reference, still reads both accumulators and returns true. A truncated record returns false. Test 28: a city saved with period 6 (no tuning exemplar, blocksPerMonth 170, iterator index 170 after one month) and loaded with the shipped tuning keeps period 6 until Init, which re-reads the tuning (period 24, blocksPerMonth 42) and resets the iterator (index 0, 1023 rand() calls for the reshuffle), and recomputes propagation from the city.",
  "steps": [
